"Estados Unidos: agencias federales, flujo SNAP-R y contactos verificados"

#: ../../book/comparison.rst:120
msgid ""
"In the United States, dual-use hardware, software, and technology export "
"licensing is administered federally by the **Bureau of Industry and Security"
" (BIS)** within the **U.S. Department of Commerce**, with zero government "
"filing fee for electronic submissions `EAR734 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ `EAR742 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/742>`_ `SNAPR "
"<https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_."
msgstr ""
"En Estados Unidos, las licencias de exportación para hardware, software y "
"tecnologías de doble uso son administradas a escala federal por la  "
"**Oficina de Industria y Seguridad (BIS)**  del  **Departamento de Comercio "
"de EE. UU.** , sin tasa administrativa alguna para las presentaciones "
"electrónicas `EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ `EAR742 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/742>`_ `SNAPR "
"<https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_."

#: ../../book/comparison.rst:122
msgid "Four Steps to Classify or Obtain US Export Approval"
msgstr ""
"Cuatro pasos para clasificar u obtener aprobación de exportación en EE. UU."

#: ../../book/comparison.rst:125
msgid ""
"**Step 1: Establish jurisdiction and publication status:** Check the exact "
"artifact under 734.3, 734.7, 734.8 and the 4E091 notes. Qualifying published"
" material can be outside the EAR; an item that is merely eligible for no "
"license to one destination can still be subject to the EAR. Part 744 "
"requirements generally concern items subject to the EAR, while other "
"sanctions and US-person rules require separate analysis. `EAR734 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ `EAR744 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/744>`_ `EAR774 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_"
msgstr ""
" **Primero, jurisdicción y publicación:**  Comprobamos 734.3, 734.7, 734.8 y"
" 4E091. Material publicado puede quedar fuera de EAR; un artículo sin "
"licencia para un destino aún puede estar sujeto. Parte744 suele tratar "
"artículos sujetos; sanciones y reglas de personas estadounidenses requieren "
"otro análisis. `EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ `EAR744 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/744>`_ `EAR774 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_"

#: ../../book/comparison.rst:126
msgid ""
"**Step 2: Obtain a Company Identification Number (CIN) on SNAP-R:** Parties "
"exporting controlled hardware (``3A090``), chip equipment, or private "
"controlled technology register online for a CIN on BIS's **Simplified "
"Network Application Process Redesign (SNAP-R)** portal at "
"``https://snapr.bis.gov`` (US-located parties submit Export License "
"applications, while parties abroad may submit Reexport License or Commodity "
"Classification requests) `EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_"
" `SNAPR <https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_."
msgstr ""
" **Paso 2: Obtener un Número de Identificación de Empresa (CIN) en SNAP-R:**"
"  Quienes exporten hardware controlado (``3A090``), maquinaria de "
"semiconductores o tecnología privada controlada deben registrarse en línea "
"para obtener un CIN en el portal  **Simplified Network Application Process "
"Redesign (SNAP-R)**  del BIS en ``https://snapr.bis.gov`` (las entidades "
"ubicadas en EE. UU. presentan solicitudes de Licencia de Exportación; las "
"situadas en el exterior pueden presentar solicitudes de Licencia de "
"Reexportación o de Clasificación de Mercancías) `EAR734 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ `SNAPR "
"<https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_."

#: ../../book/comparison.rst:127
msgid ""
"**Step 3: File a Commodity Classification (CCATS) or Policy Inquiry if "
"uncertain:** Submit technical specifications as a Commodity Classification "
"Work Item on ``snapr.bis.gov`` to receive an official ECCN determination "
"(``ACN`` tracking number), or contact BIS's Regulatory Policy Division for "
"rule interpretation `EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ "
"`SNAPR <https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_."
msgstr ""
" **Paso 3: Presentar una Clasificación Oficial (CCATS) o consulta normativa "
"en caso de duda:**  Envíe las especificaciones técnicas como solicitud de "
"clasificación en ``snapr.bis.gov`` para recibir una determinación oficial de"
" código ECCN (con número de seguimiento ``ACN``), o consulte a la División "
"de Política Regulatoria del BIS `EAR734 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_ `SNAPR "
"<https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_."

#: ../../book/comparison.rst:128
msgid ""
"**Step 4: Submit License Application & Track via STELA:** Upload PDF "
"supporting documents, end-user statements, and technical specs (for January "
"2026 China/Macau chip reviews under ``742.6(b)(10)``, attach certifications "
"of ``TPP < 21,000``, ``DRAM bandwidth < 6,500 GB/s``, US supply adequacy, "
"KYC security, and independent US lab verification) `US26 "
"<https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-01-15/html/2026-00789.htm>`_ "
"`EAR742 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/742>`_ `SNAPR "
"<https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_. Track status on **STELA** "
"(``https://snapr.bis.gov/public/stela``) `EAR734 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_."
msgstr ""
" **Paso 4: Presentar la solicitud de licencia y seguirla en STELA:**  "
"Adjunte en PDF la documentación justificativa, declaraciones de usuario "
"final y fichas técnicas (para las revisiones de chips hacia China/Macao de "
"enero de 2026 bajo ``742.6(b)(10)``, incluya las certificaciones de ``TPP < "
"21,000``, ``DRAM bandwidth < 6,500 GB/s``, suficiencia de suministro interno"
" en EE. UU., seguridad KYC y verificación por laboratorio independiente "
"estadounidense) `US26 "
"<https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-01-15/html/2026-00789.htm>`_ "
"`EAR742 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/742>`_ `SNAPR "
"<https://snapr.bis.gov/help/SNAPR-FAQ.pdf>`_. Siga el estado del expediente "
"en  **STELA**  (``https://snapr.bis.gov/public/stela``) `EAR734 "
"<https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_."

